OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The inflation rate has risen from 4.8
OL,6, per cent for July to 5.7 per cent in
OL,7, the 12 months to August.
OL,9,FEmployment Secretary Mr Norman Fowler
OL,10,Fblamed the increasing cost of mortgages
OL,11,Fbut added that high interest rates
OL,12,Fwould eventually bring the rate down.
OL,14,FInflation has been rising since the
OL,15,Fbeginning of the year, when it was 3.3
OL,16,Fper cent, but has not been above five
OL,17,Fper cent since February 1986.
OL,19,FSome City analysts now calculate that
OL,20,Finflation will almost have doubled by
OL,21,Fnext spring.
OL,23,T]CFrom 16-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18103
SC,0003
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1789594434
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G3/8
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Shadow Chancellor Mr John Smith has
OL,6, launched a stinging attack on the
OL,7, Government's economic strategy in the
OL,8, wake of the inflation rate rise.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FMr Smith said the Chancellor was guilty
OL,11,Fof "mismanagement" of the economy.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FHe forecast new public spending cuts
OL,14,Fand a growing north-south divide,
OL,15,Fadding that Mr Lawson's tax policy was
OL,16,F"a reckless folly".
OL,17,F
OL,18,F"There is 'loadsamoney' for any private
OL,19,Ffolly or extravagance but little for
OL,20,Fvital public services," Mr Smith said.
OL,21,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 16-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18104
SC,0004
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1789594434
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/8
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Hurricane Gilbert, which has claimed
OL,6, at least 58 lives so far, has turned
OL,7, south again and has hit the east
OL,8, Mexican state of Tamaulpias.
OL,10,FMexico's Yucatan peninsula was caught
OL,11,Fby the hurricane's sweep on Wednesday
OL,12,Fand the region has now been declared
OL,13,Fa national disaster area.
OL,15,FThe hurricane's force has lessened
OL,16,Fsince winds of up to 250 miles an hour
OL,17,Fblew across the Cayman Islands.
OL,19,FA state of emergency has been declared
OL,20,Fin Jamaica where 26 people were killed
OL,21,Fand one in five homes were destroyed.
OL,23,T]CFrom 16-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18105
SC,0005
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1789594434
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/8
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Whitehall sources have confirmed that
OL,6, attempts were made to persuade a Cuban
OL,7, diplomat, expelled earlier this week,
OL,8, to defect.
OL,10,FThird Secretary at the Cuban embassy
OL,11,FMr Manuel Medina Perez opened fire
OL,12,Fon a group of men in west London.
OL,14,FHe said the men had followed him and
OL,15,Fthat he believed himself to be in some
OL,16,Fdanger. Both he and the Cuban
OL,17,Fambassador were expelled from Britain.
OL,19,FA BBC correspondent says his sources
OL,20,Fsaid MI5 was involved. The Government
OL,21,Fhas made no comment on the allegations.
OL,23,T]CFrom 16-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18106
SC,0006
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1789594434
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/8
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, British Coal is on target to break even
OL,6, for the first time in 11 years, says
OL,7, the company's chairman.
OL,9,FSpeaking in Nottingham, Sir Robert
OL,10,FHaslam said the "dramatic turnaround"
OL,11,Fhad been brought about by improved
OL,12,Fproductivity and a trimmed workforce.
OL,13,F
OL,14,FSir Robert told the North Midlands Coal
OL,15,FIndustry Society that an operating
OL,16,Fprofit of #500 million was in prospect.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FBut this would only just cover BC's
OL,19,Fmassive interest burden, he said. The
OL,20,Ffigures make BC a stronger candidate
OL,21,Ffor privatisation, he added.
OL,23,T]CFrom 16-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,182,180,120,250,0,100
PN,18107
SC,0007
CT,8,C
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F181A1789594434
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/8
OL,2,D]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,V  -,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The Post Office says only seven of its
OL,6, main sorting offices are still closed
OL,7, because of the postal strike.
OL,9,FDeliveries in many parts of the country
OL,10,Fhave resumed, but the PO estimates the
OL,11,Fbacklog of 150 million letters and
OL,12,Fparcels well take two weeks to clear.
OL,14,FPost boxes in many areas which were
OL,15,Fsealed during the strike have been
OL,16,Freopened.
OL,18,FThe main offices still striking are
OL,19,FLiverpool, Manchester, Newport, Hull,
OL,20,FCardiff, Coventry and Stockport.
OL,21,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 16-09-88   teletextarchive.com
