OL,2,Q]S5 5jj jij.j  V]D
OL,3,Q]S#!!""#"""#"! V]D WORCESTERSHIRE ARE
OL,4,V ||||||||||||||]] DTHE CHAMPIONS
OL,6,CWorcestershireFhave clinched their
OL,7,Ffirst County Championship title since
OL,8,F1974 after racing to an innings victory
OL,9,Fover Glamorgan at New Road.
OL,10,F
OL,11,FEven a vandal who poured oil and
OL,12,Fpetroleum jelly on the pitch intended
OL,13,Fto delay play by an hour failed to halt
OL,14,FWorcester's title march.
OL,15,F
OL,16,FTheir maximum 24 points saw them pip
OL,17,Flong-time leaders Kent - who also
OL,18,Fscored an innings victory over Surrey
OL,19,Fwith a day to spare - by a single point
OL,20,F
OL,21,FA devastating burst of 5-2 in 22 balls
OL,22,Fby England paceman Phil Newport allowed
OL,23,FWorcester to move in for the kill.
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
